<title>USA: Salomon Inc sells $400 mln three-year notes.</title>
<headline>Salomon Inc sells $400 mln three-year notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Salomon Inc was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>Salomon Inc is a holding company for major worldwide investment banker, market maker, and precious metals traders, plus global trader and refiner of crude oil and energy related products.</p>
<p>BORROWER SALOMON INC</p>
<p>AMT $400 MLN	 COUPON 6.70 PCT   MATURITY 7/5/2000</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.918  FIRST PAY DATE 1/5/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA1  YIELD 6.729 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>S&amp;P BBB		SPREAD 58 BP	CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678</p>
</text>
